            </note>
            <note corresp="#d288-f3" n="3" xml:id="d288-f3-content">
                <p>In a July 25 letter to Gayoso, Benedick
                    requested reassignment from the post of Coordinator of Population Affairs.
                    (Department of State, Organization and Conference Files—Meetings/Governing
                    Council 1984 Meetings/Governing Council, 1983–1984, Lot 87D37, U.S. Delegation
                        ICP, Mexico City, August 1984)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d288-f4" n="4" xml:id="d288-f4-content">
                <p>Undated, attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d288-f5" n="5" xml:id="d288-f5-content">
                <p>Dam initialed the approve option. In the
                    margin above the approve option, an unknown hand typed: “8/4/84 (leb).”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
